    "body": "## ZB Communication Orchestrator v0 — PR C\n\nOWNER-approved Variant A deterministic communication core.\n\n### Exact authority\n- Spec HEAD: `9c9f0ebbf2bd5d5dc5b21578718f1ef356e278f9`\n- Plan HEAD: `54d915d6138cb2cdc805bda44d70091d53c1da1b`\n- Foundation candidate: `a1ad3e3a86d043544fb2900aa5f2d9faecefa7ad`\n- Current authority HEAD: `9fe2ab2a443560cee7ae4570c238ba02083bab50`\n- Permanent communication PR: `#111` / DRAFT / OPEN / DO NOT MERGE\n\n### Minimal Work adapter\nNormal chat = control plane. GitHub = durable state/evidence. Work = execution plane only.\n\nObserved Work runs may omit source ID/body and may also omit event actor/type. Bodyless admission therefore works as follows:\n1. repository and PR must still be exact;\n2. if actor/type are exposed, they must be `Lester-Sparx` / `issue_comment.created` or fail closed;\n3. if actor/type are NOT_EXPOSED, bodyless delta may continue only after exactly one fresh GitHub source is selected and exact-read as `Lester-Sparx`, top-level PR #111, exact immutable body;\n4. internal router envelope may then normalize actor/type from verified source + fixed R2 trigger contract; external evidence must keep unavailable physical metadata as `NOT_EXPOSED`.\n\nDirect/non-bodyless admission remains strict.\n\n### Execution law\nAfter durable `RECEIVED` fresh-read MATCH, the same physical Work event run may execute the target logical role. Real webhook delivery ID is execution identity `work-event:<DELIVERY_ID>`. No synthetic execution IDs.\n\nLegal roles: `JINGO / LESTER / DUNCAN / DJANGO`. OWNER is human-gate-only.\n\n### Fresh verification\n- bodyless admission targeted verification: `3 passed`\n- exact HEAD `hq-validate` run `33163969199` = `SUCCESS`\n- PR OPEN / UNMERGED\n\n### Forbidden\nNo polling communication trigger. No PAT router/writer. No account switching. No auto-merge. No production activation. No canon mutation. No OWNER LOCK. No PR #103 mutation. No issue #102 proof mutation/copy.\n\nThis PR is implementation authority only; it does not activate production.",
